==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries allows two AuditEntry atoms for the same application to share an identical (entryPrevStatus, entryNewStatus) pair, simulating a duplicate/mutated entry that the append-only invariant forbids. The injection forces exactly that scenario.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoSelfApproval  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_NoSelfApproval.als
    rationale: Removing F_NoSelfApproval allows a successful PATCH operation where the caller is also the application's applicant. The injection forces an Operation with kind=PatchApplicationStatus, outcome=Success, and opCaller equal to the application's appApplicant, directly violating FR-013.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_013_NoSelfApproval
      - NoSelfMutation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_013_NoSelfApproval: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OneInFlightPerApplicant  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OneInFlightPerApplicant.als
    rationale: Removing F_OneInFlightPerApplicant allows two LoanApplication atoms to exist with the same appApplicant and both in a Pending/UnderReview status, violating the one-in-flight invariant from FR-008.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerApplicant: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly allows a non-auditor caller (e.g., a pure applicant) to successfully access GetApplicationAudit, leaking audit log existence to non-auditors in violation of FR-023.
    expected to FAIL: FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly
      - FR_023_AuditEndpointAuditorOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedAccess  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedAccess.als
    rationale: Removing F_OwnershipBasedAccess permits a pure applicant (no officer, no auditor role) to successfully GET an application they do not own, breaking the byte-equivalent no-leakage guarantee from FR-020/FR-021.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch  → runs/A-L3/mutated_F_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch.als
    rationale: Removing F_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch allows an officer who is NOT the assigned officer to successfully PATCH an application's status, violating the core assignment-control invariant of FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch, LeastPrivilege
      - FR_012_OnlyAssignedOfficerCanPatch: FAIL (expected)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

